-- the hint of B is detected against C, whichever merge made C its predecessor
[(100,10,0),(200,2,1),(300,5,2)]	1	1	1	1	1	1
-- a reset the data does not show is kept while its predecessor stays (a single array, appended arrays) and detected again when a sample lands in between
[(100,10,2),(300,15,1)]	[(100,10,2),(300,15,1),(400,20,2)]	[(100,10,2),(200,12,2),(300,15,2)]
-- which of two equal samples wins does not change the hint of the sample after them
[(50,5,0),(100,1,1),(200,2,2)]	1	1	1	1
-- an equal duplicate of the predecessor does not change the hint of the sample after it, whichever is kept
[(50,5,0),(100,1,1)]	[(50,5,0),(100,1,1)]
-- the first sample keeps its hint if its equal duplicates agree, gets an unknown one if they differ, and a gauge marker wins
[(100,1,2)]	[(100,1,0)]	[(100,1,0)]	[(100,1,0)]	[(100,1,0)]	[(100,1,3)]	[(100,1,3)]
